Login to https:\\portal.azure.com using the admin account provided by your Instructor
If nessessary complete Multi Factor Authentication Registration.

As the course covers technologies that can take between 12 to 24 hours to generate any results or be available
to configure we are going to complete the steps now to minimise wait time later.

ENABLE DEFENDER FOR CLOUD
On the Azure portal home page, type Defender in the top search bar and select Defender for Cloud.
In the Defender for Cloud portal, expand Management and then click Environment Settings.
At the bottom of the main pane expand Tenant Root Group and then select your Subscription.
(If Subscription reports as Unregistered, wait 1 min & refresh page).
At the top of the page select Enable All Plans.
In the Plan Selection popout, select Microsoft Defender for APIs Plan 1 anc click Save.
Confirm that all plans report a status of ON and click the top Save button.
After approx 2 mins you should get notifications of success.
Return to the Home page.

ENABLE MICROSOFT SENTINEL
On the Azure portal home page, type Sentinel in the top search bar and select Microsoft Sentinel.
Click +Create, and then +Create a new workspace.
Create a new Resource Group called SC500MS and in the name box type MySentinel.
Click Review & Create and after validation click Create.
Once the deployment is complete type Sentinel in the top search bar and select Microsoft Sentinel.
Click +Create, and then select MySentinel and click add.
Wait for 1 min for Sentinel to deploy.
